window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-eab0e36f812a39f9"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"save-workflows-as-skills\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">将工作流保存为技能</h1> <p>把 Codex 可以反复使用的工作流程整理成技能。</p> <p>将有效的 Codex 对话、审查规则、测试命令、发布清单、设计约定、写作示例或代码库专用脚本转化为技能，让 Codex 在今后的任务中继续使用。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>希望 Codex 再次使用的成套工作流程。</li> <li>希望使用可重复技能，而不是每次都粘贴冗长提示词的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.system/skill-creator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$skill-creator（需联网）</a></td> <td>收集工作流信息、搭建技能结构、保持主要指令简洁，并验证结果。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>根据我的上下文创建技能</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 $skill-creator 创建一个 Codex 技能，用于 [fixes failing Buildkite checks on a GitHub PR / turns PR notes into inline review comments / writes our release notes from merged PRs]\n\n创建技能时使用以下来源：\n- 有效示例：[say \"use this chat,\" link a merged PR, or paste a good Codex answer]\n- 来源：[paste a Slack thread, PR review link, runbook URL, docs URL, or ticket]\n- 代码库：[repo path, if this skill depends on one repo]\n- 可复用的脚本或命令：[test command]、[preview command]、[log-fetch script]、[release command]\n- 理想输出：[paste the Slack update, changelog entry, review comment, ticket, or final answer you want future tasks to match]\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent 技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"create-a-skill-codex-can-keep-on-hand\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">创建 Codex 可以反复使用的技能</h2> <p>技能可以为重复工作提供可复用的指令、资源和脚本。<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">技能（本地尚未收录）</a> 能够保存让 Codex 首次发挥作用的任务说明、文档、命令或示例。</p> <p>可以先从一个有效示例开始：例如帮你挑选 PR 提交记录的 Codex 对话、Notion 中的发布清单、一组有用的 PR 评论，或解释发布流程的 Slack 讨论串。</p> <p><a id=\"how-to-use\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">使用方法</h2> <ol> <li>添加你希望 Codex 使用的上下文。</li> </ol> <p>留在你想保存的 Codex 对话中，粘贴 Slack 讨论串或文档链接，并补充希望 Codex 记住的规则、命令或示例。</p> <ol> <li>运行起步提示词。</li> </ol> <p>提示词会说明你希望创建什么技能，然后让 <code>$skill-creator</code> 根据指定任务、文档、PR、命令或输出示例来创建它。</p> <ol> <li>让 Codex 创建并验证技能。</li> </ol> <p>结果应定义 <code>$skill-name</code>、说明技能在什么情况下触发，并把可复用的指令放在正确位置。</p> <p><code>~/.codex/skills</code> 中的技能可从任何代码库使用。当前代码库中的技能也可以提交到代码库，让队友一并使用。</p> <ol> <li>使用技能，再根据对话更新它。</li> </ol> <p>在下一个 PR、告警、审查、发布说明或设计任务中调用新的 <code>$skill-name</code>。如果它使用了错误的测试命令、遗漏审查规则、跳过运行手册步骤，或写出的草稿你不愿意发送，可以要求 Codex 根据这次修正更新技能。</p> <p><a id=\"provide-source-material\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">提供源材料</h2> <p>请将说明技能应如何工作的材料提供给 <code>$skill-creator</code>。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>你掌握的材料</th> <th>应提供的内容</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>希望保留的 Codex 对话工作流</strong></td> <td>留在该对话中，并说 <code>use this chat</code>（“使用此对话”）。Codex 可以把对话上下文、命令、编辑和反馈作为起点。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>文档或运行手册</strong></td> <td>粘贴发布清单、关联事件响应运行手册、附加 API PDF，或指向代码库中的 Markdown 指南。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>团队讨论</strong></td> <td>粘贴解释告警的 Slack 讨论串，链接包含前端规则的 PR 审查，或附加说明客户问题的支持对话。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>技能要复用的脚本或命令</strong></td> <td>提供测试命令、预览命令、日志获取脚本、发布脚本，或本地辅助工具。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>理想结果示例</strong></td> <td>提供已合并的 PR、最终变更日志条目、已接受的发布说明、已解决的问题、前后截图，或你希望未来 Codex 输出遵循的最终答复。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>如果材料来自 Slack、Linear、GitHub、Notion 或 Sentry，可以在 Codex 中连接相应<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件（本地尚未收录）</a>、在起步提示词中提及插件，或直接粘贴相关内容。</p> <p><a id=\"what-codex-creates\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex_1\">Codex 会创建什么</h2> <p>大多数技能从一个 <code>SKILL.md</code> 文件开始。如果工作流需要，<code>$skill-creator</code> 还可以添加较长的参考资料、脚本或资源。</p> <p><a id=\"skills-you-could-create\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">可以创建的技能示例</h2> <p>当未来任务需要遵循相同的运行手册、执行相同的 CLI、使用相同的审查标准、撰写相同风格的团队更新时，可以采用同样的模式。例如：</p> <ul> <li><strong><code>$buildkite-fix-ci</code></strong>：下载失败作业的日志、诊断问题，并提出范围最小的代码修复。</li> <li><strong><code>$fix-merge-conflicts</code></strong>：将 PR 更新到基线分支，解决冲突，并返回准确的推送命令。</li> <li><strong><code>$frontend-skill</code></strong>：保存你的界面偏好、现有组件、截图验收流程，以及润色浏览器界面的步骤。</li> <li><strong><code>$pr-review-comments</code></strong>：根据上下文和证据，撰写简明且可直接添加到 GitHub 的行内评论。</li> <li><strong><code>$web-game-prototyper</code></strong>：确定首个可玩循环、选择素材、调整游戏手感、截取截图并打磨成品。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"save-workflows-as-skills\">Save workflows as skills</h1> <p>Create a skill Codex can keep on hand for work you repeat.</p> <p>Turn a working Codex chat, review rules, test commands, release checklists, design conventions, writing examples, or repo-specific scripts into a skill Codex can use in future tasks.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Codified workflows you want Codex to use again.</li> <li>Teams that want a reusable skill instead of a long prompt pasted into every chat.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/skills/tree/main/skills/.system/skill-creator\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">$skill-creator (online)</a></td> <td>Gather information about the workflow, scaffold a skill, keep the main instructions short, and validate the result.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Create a Skill From My Context</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $skill-creator to create a Codex skill that [fixes failing Buildkite checks on a GitHub PR / turns PR notes into inline review comments / writes our release notes from merged PRs]\n\nUse these sources when creating the skill:\n- Working example: [say \"use this chat,\" link a merged PR, or paste a good Codex answer]\n- Source: [paste a Slack thread, PR review link, runbook URL, docs URL, or ticket]\n- Repo: [repo path, if this skill depends on one repo]\n- Scripts or commands to reuse: [test command], [preview command], [log-fetch script], [release command]\n- Good output: [paste the Slack update, changelog entry, review comment, ticket, or final answer you want future tasks to match]\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"create-a-skill-codex-can-keep-on-hand\">Create a skill Codex can keep on hand</h2> <p>Use skills to give Codex reusable instructions, resources, and scripts for work you repeat. A <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">skill (not in this local snapshot)</a> can preserve the task, doc, command, or example that made Codex useful the first time.</p> <p>Start with one working example: a Codex chat that cherry-picked a PR, a release checklist from Notion, a set of useful PR comments, or a Slack thread explaining a launch process.</p> <h2 id=\"how-to-use\">How to use</h2> <ol> <li>Add the context you want Codex to use.</li> </ol> <p>Stay in the Codex chat you want to preserve, paste the Slack thread or docs link, and add the rule, command, or example Codex should remember.</p> <ol> <li>Run the starter prompt.</li> </ol> <p>The prompt names the skill you want, then gives <code>$skill-creator</code> the task, doc, PR, command, or output to preserve.</p> <ol> <li>Let Codex create and validate the skill.</li> </ol> <p>The result should define the <code>$skill-name</code>, describe when it should trigger, and keep reusable instructions in the right place.</p> <p>Skills in <code>~/.codex/skills</code> are available from any repo. Skills in the current repo can be committed so teammates can use them too.</p> <ol> <li>Use the skill, then update it from the chat.</li> </ol> <p>Invoke the new <code>$skill-name</code> on the next PR, alert, review, release note, or design task. If it uses the wrong test command, misses a review rule, skips a runbook step, or writes a draft you would not send, ask Codex to add that correction to the skill.</p> <h2 id=\"provide-source-material\">Provide source material</h2> <p>Give <code>$skill-creator</code> the material that explains how the skill should work.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>What you have</th> <th>What to add</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><strong>A workflow from a Codex chat that you want to preserve</strong></td> <td>Stay in that chat and say <code>use this chat</code>. Codex can use the chat context, commands, edits, and feedback as the starting point.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Docs or a runbook</strong></td> <td>Paste the release checklist, link the incident-response runbook, attach the API PDF, or point Codex at the markdown guide in your repo.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Team conversation</strong></td> <td>Paste the Slack thread where someone explained an alert, link the PR review with frontend rules, or attach the support conversation that explains the customer problem.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>Scripts or commands the skill should reuse</strong></td> <td>Add the test command, preview command, release script, log-fetch script, or local helper command you want future Codex tasks to run.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><strong>A good result</strong></td> <td>Add the merged PR, final changelog entry, accepted launch note, resolved ticket, before/after screenshot, or final Codex answer you want future tasks to match.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>If the source is in Slack, Linear, GitHub, Notion, or Sentry, connect that tool in Codex with a <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugin (not in this local snapshot)</a>, mention it in the starter prompt, or paste the relevant part into the chat.</p> <h2 id=\"what-codex-creates\">What Codex creates</h2> <p>Most skills start as a <code>SKILL.md</code> file. <code>$skill-creator</code> can add longer references, scripts, or assets when the workflow needs them.</p> <h2 id=\"skills-you-could-create\">Skills you could create</h2> <p>Use the same pattern when future tasks should read the same runbook, run the same CLI, follow the same review rubric, write the same team update, or QA the same browser flow. For example:</p> <ul> <li><strong><code>$buildkite-fix-ci</code></strong> downloads failed job logs, diagnoses the error, and proposes the smallest code fix.</li> <li><strong><code>$fix-merge-conflicts</code></strong> checks out a GitHub PR, updates it against the base branch, resolves conflicts, and returns the exact push command.</li> <li><strong><code>$frontend-skill</code></strong> keeps Codex close to your UI taste, existing components, screenshot QA loop, asset choices, and browser polish pass.</li> <li><strong><code>$pr-review-comments</code></strong> turns review notes into concise inline comments with the right tone and GitHub links.</li> <li><strong><code>$web-game-prototyper</code></strong> scopes the first playable loop, chooses assets, tunes game feel, captures screenshots, and polishes in the browser.</li> </ul>"};
